 "notes": "4 sheets (Views A-D), all checked. Units: note 6 'UNITS: INCHES'. Notes 1-6 on sheet 1 (text); note 5 is one note with four sub-paragraphs ('PLACE DATUM FEATURE A AGAINST DATUM FEATURE SIMULATOR A.', 'ENGAGE DATUM FEATURES B AND C WITH DATUM FEATURE SIMULATORS B AND C RESPECTIVELY.', 'APPLY LOAD TO PART TO RESTRAIN DATUM FEATURE A AGAINST ITS SIMULATOR.', 'DETAILED INSPECTION PLAN NEEDED TO COMPLETELY DEFINE RESTRAINT.') - recorded as ONE row (its first sentence). Note 4 (profile .06 A B C + 'APPLIES TO ALL UNTOLERANCED SURFACES.') recorded as note, tolerance.general and gdt.frame. Dimension and frame text is geometry (file class 'curves'). Modifiers: frames carrying free state (F) or tangent plane (T) have NO modifiers field (sheet 1: position Ø.023(M)(F) A B C, Ø.020(M)(F) A B, perpendicularity Ø.015(M)(F) A, flatness .03(F) over .015 on datum A; sheet 2: parallelism .015(T) D, parallelism .015(T) A, parallelism .03(F)(T) A). Two-row frames are recorded as two frames each (sheet 1 parallelism .02 D over profile .06 A B C; sheet 2 parallelism .015(T) D over profile .035 D B C, parallelism .03 A over profile .06 A B C on datum D, composite position Ø.04(M)/Ø.02(M) D B C on '10X Ø.213 +.005 -.001'; sheet 3 composite profile .040/.005 D B C all-around; sheet 4 four composite position frames Ø.050(M)/Ø.020(M) D B C with 'SIM REQT 1' (datums H, J) and 'SIM REQT 2' (K, L)). Profile .04 D E-F (sheet 2) and .015 D G(M) (sheet 3) carry the all-around circle; profile .015 D H(M)-J(M) and .015 D K(M) L(M) on sheet 4 (datum-reference modifiers not encoded). Flatness .015 on sheet 2 has the between indicator L1<->L2 (L1/L2 are region labels, not datums). '(□1.100)' is a reference square size, recorded as a reference linear dimension. tolerance.tightest: band .006 (+.005/-.001 on several sizes). Naming rule used for Ø callouts: a callout with an 'nX' count, THRU / depth, or an uppercase (hole) fit is recorded as hole.diameter {diameter, count, upper, lower}; any other Ø size is a dimension {type:'diameter'}. Tolerances are recorded as signed deviations upper/lower; limit dimensions as max/min. GD&T: characteristic in words, datums = the datum letters in order (datum-reference modifiers not encoded), modifiers 'MMC' / 'LMC' = circled M / L after the tolerance value, diameterZone true only where Ø precedes the tolerance."
}